                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3b85db1-7a2a-36d4-beb3-a040f384aea3",
                        "entry_id": "b0d2ac35-0e5c-3c4b-9948-e04d42ce0d34",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. ручное огнестрельное оружие с фитильным замком, из которого стреляли с подставки и которое наиболее активно применялось в Европе в XVI–XVIII веках"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5931ebec-012b-400d-929f-5bb6c906222e",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0d2ac35-0e5c-3c4b-9948-e04d42ce0d34",
                        "source_sense_id": "c3b85db1-7a2a-36d4-beb3-a040f384aea3",
                        "target_lang_word": "musket",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "musket",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af434c0d-bcf0-3a21-9243-eee04e225fbe",
                                        "entry_id": "9b1654cb-231e-34ae-bee2-8127b23b55ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of firearm formerly carried by the infantry of an army, originally fired by means of a match, or matchlock, for which several mechanical appliances (including the flintlock, and finally the percussion lock) were successively substituted; ultimately superseded by the rifle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2997e13-31b7-4727-9be4-0bff8de2c433",
                                                "sense_id": "af434c0d-bcf0-3a21-9243-eee04e225fbe",
                                                "text": "Soldier, soldier, won't you marry me, with your musket, fife and drum."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcf3f5fb-5def-4862-a3bd-4b74410e3112",
                                                "sense_id": "af434c0d-bcf0-3a21-9243-eee04e225fbe",
                                                "text": "Sam, Sam, pick up thy musket."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae9fa141-9ea1-4f07-b2cb-a2be56ad3790",
                                                "sense_id": "af434c0d-bcf0-3a21-9243-eee04e225fbe",
                                                "text": "[…] you may be assured, had they known the terrour of Muskets, Caliuers and Piſtols, they would haue vſed the leſſe Bowes, Speares and Bills; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8cf6571-ec5d-44ea-be4f-f762b86d7587",
                                                "sense_id": "af434c0d-bcf0-3a21-9243-eee04e225fbe",
                                                "text": "The Souldier having his Musket ſhoulder'd, muſt ſtand ſtraight upon his Limbs, hold up his Head, and look always to the commanding Officer, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51c6eba0-99cf-491d-8af3-fb50efa8c225",
                                                "sense_id": "af434c0d-bcf0-3a21-9243-eee04e225fbe",
                                                "text": "The whole of the tumultuous scene vanished from the senses of Lionel at the flash of the musket of this man, and he sunk beneath the feet of the combatants, insensible of further triumph, and of every danger."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35656ad2-d04e-4642-8ac6-e4bfb040bc33",
                                                "sense_id": "af434c0d-bcf0-3a21-9243-eee04e225fbe",
                                                "text": "Probably, rifling evolved from the early observation of the feathers on an arrow-and from the practical results of cutting channels in a musket, originally to reduce fouling, then because it was found to improve accuracy of the shot."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b4ec427-983e-3fd2-9b31-43a76556b400",
                                        "entry_id": "9b1654cb-231e-34ae-bee2-8127b23b55ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male Eurasian sparrowhawk (Accipiter nisus)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8cadd20c-1759-4826-b19e-d75c2a1791a7",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0d2ac35-0e5c-3c4b-9948-e04d42ce0d34",
